\f[B]stdout\f[R] = \f[I]string\f[R], default \f[CR]\(dq\(dq\f[R]
Not used.
.SS Disks
The disks are in the subtables \f[B]disks.hda\f[R], \f[B]disks.hdb\f[R],
\f[B]disks.hdc\f[R], \f[B]disks.hdd\f[R], \f[B]disks.fda\f[R],
\f[B]disks.fdb\f[R] and \f[B]disks.mtdblock\f[R], one for each device,
all of them always written:
.TP
\f[B]disks.\f[R]\f[I]device\f[R]\f[B].image\f[R] = \f[I]image\f[R], default \f[CR]\(dq\(dq\f[R]
The image of the device, by name.
.TP
\f[B]disks.\f[R]\f[I]device\f[R]\f[B].private\f[R] = \f[I]boolean\f[R], default \f[CR]false\f[R]
Write to a private copy\-on\-write file,
\f[I]vm\f[R]_\f[I]device\f[R].cow in the project directory, instead of
the image, which then stays unchanged.
The format of the file is the project\(aqs \f[B]cowfmt\f[R].
.SS Network cards
\f[B]nics\f[R] is an array of tables, the network cards in the order the
guest sees them.
Each card has these keys:
.TP
\f[B]kind\f[R] = \f[I]choice\f[R]
\f[B]\(dqplug\(dq\f[R] for a card plugged into a socket,
\f[B]\(dqsocket\(dq\f[R] for a card that other bricks plug into, or
\f[B]\(dqhostonly\(dq\f[R] for a card on QEMU\(aqs user networking.
.TP
\f[B]connect\f[R] = \f[I]string\f[R]
With \f[B]\(dqplug\(dq\f[R], the socket the card is plugged into; see
\f[B]Connections\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]name\f[R] = \f[I]string\f[R]
With \f[B]\(dqsocket\(dq\f[R], the name of the socket card, made of
letters, digits, underscores, hyphens and dots.
Other bricks connect to it as \f[I]vm\f[R]:\f[I]name\f[R].
When it\(aqs missing, the card is named \f[B]sock_eth\f[R]\f[I]N\f[R]
after its position.
.TP
\f[B]model\f[R] = \f[I]string\f[R], default \f[CR]\(dqrtl8139\(dq\f[R]
The model of the card, for example \f[B]\(dqe1000\(dq\f[R] or
\f[B]\(dqvirtio\-net\-pci\(dq\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]mac\f[R] = \f[I]string\f[R]
The MAC address, as \f[B]\(dq52:54:00:12:34:56\(dq\f[R].
A missing or invalid address is replaced with a random one.
.SS switch
A VDE switch, \f[B]vde_switch\f[R](1).
Plugs connect to it by its name.
.TP
\f[B]numports\f[R] = \f[I]integer\f[R] 1\-128, default \f[CR]32\f[R]
The number of ports.
.TP
\f[B]hub\f[R] = \f[I]boolean\f[R], default \f[CR]false\f[R]
Send every packet to every port, like a hub.
.TP
\f[B]fstp\f[R] = \f[I]boolean\f[R], default \f[CR]false\f[R]
Enable the fast spanning tree protocol.
.SS switchwrapper
A VDE switch that Virtualbricks doesn\(aqt start, run by another
program.
Plugs connect to it by its name.
.TP
\f[B]path\f[R] = \f[I]path\f[R], default \f[CR]\(dq\(dq\f[R]
The control directory of the switch.
.SS tap
A tap interface of the host, plugged into a switch through
\f[B]vde_plug2tap\f[R](1).
It needs privileges, see \f[B]sudo\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]connect\f[R] = \f[I]string\f[R], default \f[CR]\(dq\(dq\f[R]
The socket the tap is plugged into.
.TP
\f[B]mode\f[R] = \f[I]choice\f[R], default \f[CR]\(dqoff\(dq\f[R]
How the interface gets its address: \f[B]\(dqoff\(dq\f[R] for not at
all, \f[B]\(dqdhcp\(dq\f[R], or \f[B]\(dqmanual\(dq\f[R] for
\f[B]ip\f[R], \f[B]nm\f[R] and \f[B]gw\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]ip\f[R] = \f[I]address\f[R], default \f[CR]\(dq10.0.0.1\(dq\f[R]
The address of the interface.
.TP
\f[B]nm\f[R] = \f[I]address\f[R], default \f[CR]\(dq255.255.255.0\(dq\f[R]
The netmask.
.TP
\f[B]gw\f[R] = \f[I]address\f[R], default \f[CR]\(dq\(dq\f[R]
The default gateway, or empty for none.
.SS capture
Captures the packets of an interface of the host into a switch, through
\f[B]vde_pcapplug\f[R].
It needs privileges, see \f[B]sudo\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]connect\f[R] = \f[I]string\f[R], default \f[CR]\(dq\(dq\f[R]
The socket the capture is plugged into.
.TP
\f[B]iface\f[R] = \f[I]string\f[R], default \f[CR]\(dq\(dq\f[R]
The interface of the host, for example \f[B]\(dqeth0\(dq\f[R].
.SS wire
Connects two sockets, through \f[B]dpipe\f[R](1) and
\f[B]vde_plug\f[R](1).
.TP
\f[B]endpoints\f[R] = \f[I]array\f[R], default \f[CR][\(dq\(dq, \(dq\(dq]\f[R]
The two sockets, left and right.
.SS netemu
A wire that emulates a network link: bandwidth, delay, buffer and loss,
which can change over time between the states of a Markov chain.
.TP
\f[B]endpoints\f[R] = \f[I]array\f[R], default \f[CR][\(dq\(dq, \(dq\(dq]\f[R]
The two sockets, left and right.
LR values apply from left to right, RL values from right to left.
.TP
\f[B]transperiod\f[R] = \f[I]integer\f[R] >= 1, default \f[CR]100\f[R]
How often the emulator may change state, in milliseconds.
.TP
\f[B]transitions\f[R] = \f[I]array\f[R], default \f[CR][[0.0]]\f[R]
The transition matrix: the number in row \f[I]i\f[R] and column
\f[I]j\f[R] is the probability of going from state \f[I]i\f[R] to state
\f[I]j\f[R] at each period.
It has a row and a column for each state.
.PP
\f[B]states\f[R] is an array of tables, at least one, and the first one
is the state the emulator starts in.
Each state has these keys:
.TP
\f[B]name\f[R] = \f[I]string\f[R], default \f[CR]\(dqdefault name\(dq\f[R]
The name of the state.
.TP
\f[B]bandwidth\f[R] = \f[I]integer\f[R], default \f[CR]125000\f[R]
The bandwidth, in bytes per second, or 0 for no limit; from left to
right when \f[B]bandwidthsymm\f[R] is false.
.TP
\f[B]bandwidthr\f[R] = \f[I]integer\f[R], default \f[CR]125000\f[R]
The bandwidth from right to left.
.TP
\f[B]bandwidthsymm\f[R] = \f[I]boolean\f[R], default \f[CR]true\f[R]
Use \f[B]bandwidth\f[R] in both directions.
.TP
\f[B]delay\f[R] = \f[I]integer\f[R], default \f[CR]0\f[R]
The propagation delay, one way, in milliseconds; from left to right when
\f[B]delaysymm\f[R] is false.
.TP
\f[B]delayr\f[R] = \f[I]integer\f[R], default \f[CR]0\f[R]
The delay from right to left.
.TP
\f[B]delaysymm\f[R] = \f[I]boolean\f[R], default \f[CR]true\f[R]
Use \f[B]delay\f[R] in both directions.
.TP
\f[B]chanbufsize\f[R] = \f[I]integer\f[R], default \f[CR]75000\f[R]
The size of the channel buffer, in bytes, or 0 for no limit; from left
to right when \f[B]chanbufsizesymm\f[R] is false.
.TP
\f[B]chanbufsizer\f[R] = \f[I]integer\f[R], default \f[CR]75000\f[R]
The size of the channel buffer from right to left.
.TP
\f[B]chanbufsizesymm\f[R] = \f[I]boolean\f[R], default \f[CR]true\f[R]
Use \f[B]chanbufsize\f[R] in both directions.
.TP
\f[B]loss\f[R] = \f[I]number\f[R] 0\-100, default \f[CR]0.0\f[R]
The percentage of packets lost; from left to right when
\f[B]losssymm\f[R] is false.
.TP
\f[B]lossr\f[R] = \f[I]number\f[R] 0\-100, default \f[CR]0.0\f[R]
The percentage of packets lost from right to left.
.TP
\f[B]losssymm\f[R] = \f[I]boolean\f[R], default \f[CR]true\f[R]
Use \f[B]loss\f[R] in both directions.
.SS tunnellisten
The server end of an encrypted tunnel between two machines, through
\f[B]vde_cryptcab\f[R](1).
.TP
\f[B]connect\f[R] = \f[I]string\f[R], default \f[CR]\(dq\(dq\f[R]
The socket the tunnel is plugged into.
.TP
\f[B]port\f[R] = \f[I]integer\f[R] 1\-65535, default \f[CR]7667\f[R]
The UDP port to listen on.
.TP
\f[B]password\f[R] = \f[I]string\f[R], default \f[CR]\(dq\(dq\f[R]
The password of the tunnel.
It\(aqs stored in clear text.
.SS tunnelconnect
The client end of an encrypted tunnel, through
\f[B]vde_cryptcab\f[R](1).
.TP
\f[B]connect\f[R] = \f[I]string\f[R], default \f[CR]\(dq\(dq\f[R]
The socket the tunnel is plugged into.
.TP
\f[B]host\f[R] = \f[I]string\f[R], default \f[CR]\(dq\(dq\f[R]
The host that runs the server end.
.TP
\f[B]port\f[R] = \f[I]integer\f[R] 1\-65535, default \f[CR]7667\f[R]
The UDP port of the server end.
.TP
\f[B]localport\f[R] = \f[I]integer\f[R] 1\-65535, default \f[CR]10771\f[R]
The local UDP port.
.TP
\f[B]password\f[R] = \f[I]string\f[R], default \f[CR]\(dq\(dq\f[R]
The password of the tunnel.
It\(aqs stored in clear text.
.SS router
A router.
It has only the two event keys.
.SH MIGRATION
The first time Virtualbricks starts after an upgrade from 2.1 or older,
it converts \f[I]\(ti/.virtualbricks.conf\f[R] into
\f[B]settings.toml\f[R] and \f[B]state.toml\f[R], and the
\f[I].project\f[R] file of each project into a \f[B]project.toml\f[R]
next to it, and shows what it converted in a window.
The old files are left as they were.
.PP
The same conversion can be tried on copies, into a new folder laid out
like the XDG directories:
.IP
.EX
python \-m virtualbricks.migrate \-\-settings \(ti/.virtualbricks.conf \(rs
    \(ti/vb\-copy /tmp/vb\-test
.EE
.PP
\f[B]virtualbricks\-migrate\f[R] opens the same conversion in a window,
and \f[B]python \-m virtualbricks.migrate \-\-help\f[R] lists every
option.
An archive of an old project is converted when it\(aqs imported.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[I]$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\f[R]/virtualbricks/settings.toml
The settings.
.TP
\f[I]$XDG_STATE_HOME\f[R]/virtualbricks/state.toml
The state.
.TP
\f[I]$XDG_STATE_HOME\f[R]/virtualbricks/migration\-report.txt
The report of the last migration.
.TP
\f[I]workspace\f[R]/\f[I]project\f[R]/project.toml
A project.
.TP
\f[I]workspace\f[R]/vimages/
The images saved when a project is imported.
.TP
\f[I]$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\f[R]/virtualbricks/\f[I]project\f[R]/
The sockets and consoles of the running bricks, removed when you log
out.
.TP
\f[I]/tmp/vb.lock\f[R]
The lock that lets only one Virtualbricks run on the machine.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\f[B]XDG_CONFIG_HOME\f[R], \f[B]XDG_STATE_HOME\f[R]
Where the settings and the state are, \f[I]\(ti/.config\f[R] and
\f[I]\(ti/.local/state\f[R] when they are not set.
Relative paths are ignored, as the XDG Base Directory specification
says.
.TP
\f[B]XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\f[R]
Where the sockets are.
When it\(aqs not set, they are in a directory
\f[I]virtualbricks\-\f[R]uid of the temporary directory, readable only
by you.
.SH EXAMPLES
A \f[B]settings.toml\f[R] as Virtualbricks writes it at its first start:
.IP
.EX
format = 1
cowfmt = \(dqqcow2\(dq
erroronloop = false
femaleplugs = false
qemupath = \(dq/usr/bin\(dq
vdepath = \(dq/usr/bin\(dq
workspace = \(dq/home/alice/.virtualbricks\(dq
term = \(dq/usr/bin/xterm\(dq
sudo = \(dq/usr/bin/gksu\(dq
ksm = false
systray = true
show_missing = true
.EE
.PP
A \f[B]project.toml\f[R] with a virtual machine, two switches connected
by a network emulator with two states, a tap and an event.
The virtual machine is shortened: Virtualbricks writes all of its keys,
and the six empty disks.
.IP
.EX
format = 1

[settings]
cowfmt = \(dqqcow2\(dq
erroronloop = false
femaleplugs = false
qemupath = \(dq/usr/bin\(dq
vdepath = \(dq/usr/bin\(dq

[images.debian]
path = \(dq/home/alice/.virtualbricks/vimages/debian\-12.qcow2\(dq
description = \(dqDebian 12\(rsnbase image\(dq

[events.start_lab]
actions = [
    {kind = \(dqvb\(dq, command = \(dqsw1 on\(dq},
    {kind = \(dqshell\(dq, command = \(dqlogger lab started\(dq},
]
delay = 5

[bricks.sw1]
type = \(dqswitch\(dq
pon_vbevent = \(dqstart_lab\(dq
poff_vbevent = \(dq\(dq
numports = 16
hub = false
fstp = true

[bricks.sw2]
type = \(dqswitch\(dq
pon_vbevent = \(dq\(dq
poff_vbevent = \(dq\(dq
numports = 32
hub = false
fstp = false

[bricks.router1]
type = \(dqqemu\(dq
pon_vbevent = \(dq\(dq
poff_vbevent = \(dq\(dq
argv0 = \(dqqemu\-system\-x86_64\(dq
kvm = true
smp = 2
ram = 1024
# ... and the other keys of a qemu brick

[bricks.router1.disks.hda]
image = \(dqdebian\(dq
private = true

# ... and hdb to mtdblock, with image = \(dq\(dq and private = false

[[bricks.router1.nics]]
kind = \(dqplug\(dq
connect = \(dqsw1\(dq
model = \(dqe1000\(dq
mac = \(dq52:54:00:12:34:01\(dq

[[bricks.router1.nics]]
kind = \(dqhostonly\(dq
model = \(dqvirtio\-net\-pci\(dq
mac = \(dq52:54:00:12:34:02\(dq

[[bricks.router1.nics]]
kind = \(dqsocket\(dq
name = \(dqlan\(dq
model = \(dqe1000\(dq
mac = \(dq52:54:00:12:34:03\(dq

[bricks.tap0]
type = \(dqtap\(dq
pon_vbevent = \(dq\(dq
poff_vbevent = \(dq\(dq
ip = \(dq10.0.0.1\(dq
nm = \(dq255.255.255.0\(dq
gw = \(dq\(dq
mode = \(dqmanual\(dq
connect = \(dqsw2\(dq

[bricks.wan]
type = \(dqnetemu\(dq
pon_vbevent = \(dq\(dq
poff_vbevent = \(dq\(dq
transperiod = 100
transitions = [[0.0, 0.2], [0.5, 0.0]]
endpoints = [\(dqsw1\(dq, \(dqsw2\(dq]

[[bricks.wan.states]]
name = \(dqgood\(dq
bandwidth = 125000
bandwidthr = 125000
bandwidthsymm = true
delay = 10
delayr = 0
delaysymm = true
chanbufsize = 75000
chanbufsizer = 75000
chanbufsizesymm = true
loss = 0.0
lossr = 0.0
losssymm = true

[[bricks.wan.states]]
name = \(dqcongested\(dq
bandwidth = 125000
bandwidthr = 125000
bandwidthsymm = true
delay = 200
delayr = 50
delaysymm = false
chanbufsize = 75000
chanbufsizer = 75000
chanbufsizesymm = true
loss = 2.5
lossr = 0.0
losssymm = true
.EE
.SH BUGS
The \f[B]mode\f[R], \f[B]ip\f[R], \f[B]nm\f[R] and \f[B]gw\f[R] of a tap
are stored but not applied: the interface gets no address from
Virtualbricks.
